     "nodeId": "p11-sector-definition-content",
     "replacement": "The radian formula for sector area is simpler than the degree formula. This simplicity is needed later in calculus.\n\n**Sector area using degrees**\t**Sector area using radians**\t[tikz]\n% mathsmap-inline-width-mm 41.1\n% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"sectorFill\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"identifies the sector whose area is A\"}],\"reference\":\"page 11 sector area formula diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{sectorFill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (R) at (2,0);\n\\coordinate (P) at (130:2);\n\\path[fill=sectorFill] (O)--(R) arc[start angle=0,end angle=130,radius=2]--cycle;\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (O) circle[radius=2];\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (P)--(O)--(R);\n\\path (O)--(R) node[midway,below] {\\$r\\$};\n\\path (O)--(P) node[midway,left] {\\$r\\$};\n\\node at (65:0.38) {\\$\\theta\\$};\n\\node at (65:1.16) {\\$A\\$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\n$$A=\\frac{\\theta}{360^{\\circ}}\\times\\pi r^2$$\t$$A=\\frac12r^2\\theta$$ $\\theta$ is in radians.\n\n$A$: sector area\n$r$: radius\n$\\theta$: angle at the centre",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p11-sector-definition",
